{"schema":1,"function":"levy_ppf","description":"Levy distribution quantile function mu + c / (2 erfc^-1(p)^2)","inputs":["mu","c","p"],"outputs":["y"],"points":180,"tolerance":{"rel":1e-13,"reason":"p is an exact double; a careful method forms erfc^-1(p) within a few ulps (Boost's erf_inv reaches about 1e-16; 1 - p is exact for p >= 1/2), then c / (2 y^2) costs a few ulps more and mu + c / (2 y^2) costs (|mu| + |c / (2 y^2)|) / |x| ulps, at most about 7.2 on this grid (tested), 8e-16; it is exactly mu at p = 0. 1e-13 as for the other quantiles"},"grid":"(mu, c) in {(0, 1), (0, 2^-500), (0, 2^500), (-10, 1/4), (100, 8), (-2^1023, 2^1023)} x the gamma_ppf probabilities (p = 0, 5e-324, 1e-300, 1e-100, 1e-50, 1e-20, 1e-10, 1e-5, 1e-3, 0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.25, 0.4, 1/2 - 1e-10, 1/2, 1/2 + 1e-10, 0.6, 0.75, 0.9, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999, 1 - 1e-5, 1 - 1e-10, 1 - 1e-15 and 1) and the doubles next to 1/2 (1/2 - 2^-54, 1/2 + 2^-53) and 1 (1 - 2^-53); the quantile is mu at p = 0, p = 1 is tagged pole (+inf), quantiles beyond the largest double are tagged overflow","mpmath":{"version":"1.4.1","dps":[50,100]},"scipy":{"version":"1.18.1","function":"scipy.stats.levy.ppf"},"numpy":"2.5.4","python":"3.13"}
